shown that consistently under consuming

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:41.910
calories can significantly decrease the
number of calories that your body burns.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:46.650
A great example of this is
the biggest loser research. While of

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:49.770
course it's expected that the number of
calories that your body needs to

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:54.240
maintain a lower body weight will be
fewer than the number of calories needed

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:59.280
to maintain a higher body weight, what
wasn't expected and what was found in

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:04.500
the research was the additional 500
calorie reduction in resting metabolic

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:11.840
rate. In other words, as an example, if you
needed 2,000 calories to hold steady at

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:18.810
150 pounds, for example, maybe you would
be expected to need 1,500 calories to

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:23.850
hold steady at 130 pounds. But what they
were finding was that you would actually

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:29.730
need to consume only a thousand calories
to maintain that 20-pound weight loss.

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:35.850
It's no wonder then that so many people
gain back the weight that they lose and

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:40.770
they gain more. I'm not saying this of
course to scare people who have dieted

00:11:40.770 --> 00:11:45.960
or to shame people who maybe already
feel ashamed for severely restricting

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:49.800
calories in the past. I mean this is not
