isn't enough time for nuance and context
in these videos. They're really just

00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:47.970
giving you the polished highlight reel of
what recovery can look like. I also do

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:52.980
worry that the apps algorithm might be
really dangerous for this population as

00:21:52.980 --> 00:21:58.620
just after I watched a few of these
weight loss "What I Eat In A Day" videos, I was

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:04.980
fed a ton of more problematic weight
loss and disorderly content. Now, I went

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:09.840
through TikTok's Community Guidelines
and there were actually a few terms that

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:14.700
definitely could deem these videos as
being against the Community Guidelines.

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:19.710
So for one, they actually say that they
do not permit misinformation that may

00:22:19.710 --> 00:22:25.650
cause harm to an individual's health, and
two they also do say that they do not

00:22:25.650 --> 00:22:31.740
permit any normalizing or encouraging of
triggering self-harm behavior including

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:38.340
content that supports pro-ana or other
dangerous behaviors to lose weight.

00:22:38.340 --> 00:22:43.470
I know that diet culture has us thinking
that eating less than 1000

00:22:43.470 --> 00:22:49.440
calories is "norma"l or even a "healthy"
behavior for weight loss, but I would

00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:55.200
flag all five of these videos as
violating TikTok's Terms of Use.

00:22:55.200 --> 00:22:58.320
TikTok, I mean reach out to me or really any

00:22:58.320 --> 00:23:02.220
other health professional if you need
some help identifying what is

00:23:02.220 --> 00:23:08.220
problematic and what is not because
there is a lot of content on the

00:23:08.220 --> 00:23:13.380
platform that needs to come down. I just
want to finish here by reminding you to

00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:17.970
please be kind to TikTok users who
are posting or promoting this type of

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:23.300
content. I actually don't think these
people, especially the younger users,

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:30.630
really know what is "healthy" behavior and
what is not. Ultimately, we have all been

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:37.170
socialized to believe that less is more
and are largely relying on misinformed

00:23:37.170 --> 00:23:39.900
wellness influencers for our education
on

00:23:39.900 --> 00:23:44.400
nutrition. So I actually have a tremendous
amount of empathy for these TikTokers.

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:48.390
I think everyone's just using
the coping mechanisms that we've been

00:23:48.390 --> 00:23:53.490
taught. Having said that, even if you're
not claiming to be a "wellness influencer",

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:58.770
or recommending a certain way of eating,
if you're putting content out into the

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:04.440
world you have to take responsibility
for it and expect that people are going

00:24:04.440 --> 00:24:09.510
to follow suit. I need everyone watching
right now who has a social media profile,

00:24:09.510 --> 00:24:14.970
to think really hard about everything
you put out there onto the internet that

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:20.970
people can view and see. You don't have
to be saying "do this", "do that" to cause

00:24:20.970 --> 00:24:26.130
harm. Anecdotal "success stories" are very
persuasive

00:24:26.130 --> 00:24:31.920
so just seeing one person on the
internet say" I ate this and lost this

00:24:31.920 --> 00:24:37.890
much weight" can be enough to encourage a
lot of other people to follow suit. Let's

00:24:37.890 --> 00:24:43.980
all try to be a little bit more mindful
of that. And on that note I think that is

00:24:43.980 --> 00:24:48.690
all for me. I will definitely be deleting
the app for now until we see a little

00:24:48.690 --> 00:24:52.980
better management of this type of
problematic content. So friends, if you

00:24:52.980 --> 00:24:57.420
like this video please be sure to
